# Fixed unsigned RR13 registration candidates

This inactive preparation library constructs reviewable data for RR13a/RR13b. Contract 1.0.9, its 792 units/1584 typed nodes, 55 historical records and all ownership holds remain unchanged. No default import reads files or runs application code.
`derive(files)` accepts an explicit relative-name→bytes map containing the pinned complete baseline, all old contract inputs, six preserved policies and the proposed storage lane/template/amendment. The template must state parent_intent RR13→[RR13a,RR13b]. It returns unsigned policy, expected-plan, contract and schema artifacts, preserving full old records and rebuilding typed edges with an independent cycle check.
`contract_lock(files, old_lock_bytes)` retains every old required path and adds the fixed EXTRA source/input set. Prior arguments enter the aggregate bound before hashing or parsing; the prior/ namespace is reserved. `snapshot(files, old_register_bytes, old_snapshot_lock_bytes, old_contract_lock_bytes, snapshot_id, base_main, progress_inputs=())` copies every actual generated unit field, brief hash, current integration attribution and historical acceptance value; it preserves old progress inputs and binds explicitly added ones.
All functions return UNSEALED_PROPOSAL_ONLY with complete supplied-input SHA-256 bindings. Both derive and snapshot pin the entire historical execution file, including integration and unknown attribution. They never install candidates,seal validators,invoke generators or claim source/feature acceptance. The root separately reviews unsigned actual outputs before any 1.0.10 adoption.
`emit(fresh_path, proposal)` optionally writes only named candidate JSON artifacts plus a source/input/output-bound manifest into a new owned 0700 directory under /workspace/build/builderbob. Existing/symlink/noncanonical outputs refuse. Input bytes plus canonical key/hash metadata and emitted-output framing each have a 64MiB refusal cap; this is not a sandbox or performance guarantee.
Run `python3 -I -B -m unittest discover -s porting/rust-parity-plan-20261026/composition/registration -p test_prepare.py -v` and repeat with `python3 -I -O -B -m unittest discover -s porting/rust-parity-plan-20261026/composition/registration -p test_prepare.py -v`.
Snapshot reuses the complete fixed preparation/whole storage guard after checking actual raw bytes against the supplied map/current lock. Only one strict POLICY_SHA256 literal is normalized for guard code identity; the actual verified bytes execute unchanged and cache by raw SHA. The default PENDING guard refuses snapshot; production cannot assign or override its seal.
The tests reuse the three exact captured 1.0.9 baseline JSON fixtures and old current snapshot inputs. All tiny added children,amendment, briefs and inactive code bindings are explicitly SYNTHETIC_UNSEALED controls counted as test source. They are not the complete unadopted RR13 work records and must never be installed.
Tests cover strict finite JSON,complete old record/graph restoration,private results,held inputs, source pins, caps, cycles, exact lock sets, full snapshot fields/progress and real private fresh-output/refusal controls. Tests scope and restore a synthetic sealed guard read with matching raw input/lock pins; they never edit the on-disk guard. Hosted output tests patch only OUTPUT_ROOT to their own admitted runner temporary directory; production has no path override.
Source review and root-owned normal/optimized execution remain pending. Existing 165-line current-plan storage tests, 191-line draft guard and 252-line landed guard tests retain their own roles; this library does not replace their adoption gates.
Future P2 must use the complete actual RR13 draft, independently inspect its unsigned policy,seal/pin the landed guard and module-alias shim,apply reviewed shared wiring and exact required inputs,run actual build_plan,compare all generated records/edges,then construct and verify the final snapshot. EXTRA lists the exact future adapter/source paths that must also enter the contract validator’s required set.
The full 26 original SnapshotStore cases,fault/permission/filesystem ranges,M06/M104/C01/C02/native/UI and durable application journey remain open. The complete original identity/SnapshotStore integration still requires its separate later registration; no hold or human reservation is released.
